mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">This course is part of an integrated teaching series for nursing and health management programs, breaking away from the traditional discipline-specific approach by minimizing boundaries between subjects. It systematically introduces students to the morphology and function of the normal human body to ensure a coherent and holistic learning experience. The curriculum prioritizes a macroscopic understanding of human structure and function before delving into microscopic knowledge. As the fourth module of Normal Human Morphology and Physiology, this course focuses on fundamental principles of human systematic anatomy.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
